01:11:52.660 --> 01:11:54.050
also could change a lot.

01:11:54.050 --> 01:11:55.973
We thought about that, but again,

01:11:57.170 --> 01:11:59.410
where you get data on that,

01:11:59.410 --> 01:12:01.100
that's very hard to understand.

01:12:01.100 --> 01:12:04.040
It's very difficult to get
data on that or measure it

01:12:04.040 --> 01:12:05.543
in a consistent way.

01:12:06.930 --> 01:12:08.730
I think that's an interesting
source of variation,

01:12:08.730 --> 01:12:10.280
but I haven't thought about it.

01:12:12.740 --> 01:12:15.580
I have no guesses as to what
the answer would be, yeah.

01:12:15.580 --> 01:12:18.560
- So Jim, along the same
lines, have there been any

01:12:18.560 --> 01:12:21.790
significant changes in the
technology of coca production

01:12:21.790 --> 01:12:26.790
that interacts with the
growing conditions in any way?

01:12:27.780 --> 01:12:31.723
Like makes them less relevant
or more relevant over time?

01:12:34.170 --> 01:12:36.320
- I think that's certainly true.

01:12:36.320 --> 01:12:39.720
The story in Columbia is that

01:12:39.720 --> 01:12:42.380
when Pablo Escobar and
the Medellin drug cartel,

01:12:42.380 --> 01:12:45.223
they used to buy all the
coca in Bolivia and Peru,

01:12:47.250 --> 01:12:48.440
but then they decided they just

01:12:48.440 --> 01:12:50.160
start growing it in Columbia.

01:12:50.160 --> 01:12:54.520
But the type of coca strains
that grew in Bolivia,

01:12:54.520 --> 01:12:57.280
they wanted to grow it
at much lower altitudes

01:12:57.280 --> 01:13:01.100
in the Yanos, the tropical
plains in the east,

01:13:01.100 --> 01:13:05.870
and the stuff in Chapare,
it was too high altitude.

01:13:05.870 --> 01:13:08.880
So it was too hot, basically,
where the Columbians...

01:13:08.880 --> 01:13:11.590
So then they did all this
Jeanette green engine.

01:13:11.590 --> 01:13:13.690
It was a green revolution in coca.

01:13:13.690 --> 01:13:15.390
They hired these scientists

01:13:15.390 --> 01:13:18.783
and basically bred coca that flourished.

01:13:21.281 --> 01:13:23.610
I don't know what but that's
the story that's in books

01:13:23.610 --> 01:13:25.180
about the Medellin drug cartel.

01:13:25.180 --> 01:13:27.510
I don't quite know what
the evidence for that is,

01:13:27.510 --> 01:13:29.280
but people tell that story in Columbia.

01:13:29.280 --> 01:13:33.800
So that would suggest
that maybe there's some

01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:37.270
sort of mutability in these conditions,

01:13:37.270 --> 01:13:39.010
but I don't quite know.

01:13:39.010 --> 01:13:41.176
We could dig more into the side.

01:13:41.176 --> 01:13:43.660
The FAO, that's not
the way the information

01:13:43.660 --> 01:13:45.530
is presented in the FAO data.

01:13:45.530 --> 01:13:48.200
Is that a budgerigar on your shoulder?

01:13:48.200 --> 01:13:49.033
- Yeah.

01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:52.170
- Okay, sorry.

01:13:52.170 --> 01:13:53.270
It was putting me off.

01:13:57.153 --> 01:13:58.710
So I don't know.

01:13:58.710 --> 01:14:00.250
- That makes it even more surprising,

01:14:00.250 --> 01:14:03.630
the persistent effects of the immutable

01:14:03.630 --> 01:14:05.930
portion of the conditions, right?

01:14:05.930 --> 01:14:06.763
- Yeah, I don't know.

01:14:06.763 --> 01:14:08.680
I don't know if that's
happened in Bolivia.

01:14:08.680 --> 01:14:09.910
We should ask about that.

01:14:09.910 --> 01:14:10.840
We should ask about that.

01:14:10.840 --> 01:14:12.800
I'm sure there's people
who would know in Bolivia,

01:14:12.800 --> 01:14:16.070
if that were true and I don't know.

01:14:16.070 --> 01:14:19.723
Pablo might know, but
we could ask about that.

01:14:20.690 --> 01:14:22.690
- Okay, well, we're out of time.

01:14:22.690 --> 01:14:26.120
I want to let people go if they need to.

01:14:26.120 --> 01:14:29.130
But Jim, thanks so much
for spending time with us.

01:14:29.130 --> 01:14:33.340
And it was great to have you
because it also unsurprisingly

01:14:33.340 --> 01:14:35.150
brings together people
from different disciplines

01:14:35.150 --> 01:14:36.350
and departments at Yale.

01:14:37.310 --> 01:14:38.143
- Okay.

01:14:38.143 --> 01:14:39.660
Yeah, I'm very sorry I
couldn't be there in person.

01:14:39.660 --> 01:14:41.460
That would have been very fun, yeah.

01:14:42.910 --> 01:14:43.743
